{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014NA3VjQpH8qCip4Uivkj7E","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tr\"\"\"errorlist_check - the cycle-start LabVIEW Error List check (user decision 5, 2026-09-24):\n2\t\"사이클 시작하기 전에 LabVIEW 컴파일 에러 창은 반드시 확인해야할듯. GUI로 에러 내용 확인하고 각 에러 더블클릭하면 에러\n3\t위치로 이동해서 보여주거든. (블락 다이어그램 켜진 상태에서)\".\n4\t\n5\tWHAT ALREADY EXISTS (checked first): `tools/lv_errorlist.py` reads every Error List row by capture+OCR, count-checked\n6\tagainst the window's own \"N errors and warnings\" (docs/toolkit-capabilities.md:313; test tools/bench/diag_errorlist_v0.py).\n7\tThis file REUSES it unchanged except for one optional per-item hook (`on_item`), and adds: a byte-identical SCRATCH copy\n8\t(the bed itself is never opened), Ctrl+E so the block diagram is up, a double-click per item with a capture of the\n9\tblock diagram before/after, a zero-item path for a runnable VI, the expected-errors comparison, and the cleanup proofs.\n10\tThe selected object's UID is NOT read: `TopLevelDiagram.Selection List[]` 0x6349400 exists (NI API ref) but the fleet\n11\thas no op that reads it (`grep \"Selection\" tools/gscript.py` -> 0), and branching `Open VI Reference.vi reference`\n12\tinto a VI-class property node is a MEASURED failure (docs/toolkit-capabilities.md:666). Recorded per item as uid=None.\n13\t\n14\tPREDICTION CONTRACT: Ctrl+E opens '<scratch> Block Diagram'; Ctrl+L opens a new 'Error list' window; items read ==\n15\tthe window's own N (0 for a runnable VI); each double-click fronts the block diagram and changes its capture; the\n16\tError List is closed with Esc; the scratch is closed and deleted; the bed md5 is unchanged; no VI is run or saved.\n17\tEvery GUI act goes through lv_gui.ps1 with -Exception Approved -Evidence EVID (logged to tools/gui_actions.log).\n18\t\n19\t  py tools/errorlist_check.py [--vi <bed.vi>] [--expected <file.json>]      rc 0 OK / 1 MISMATCH / 2 FAIL\n20\t  expected file: {\"expected\": [{\"match\": \"<substring of the row text>\", \"count\": n}, ...]}  (default: none = [])\n21\tLast stdout line: `ERRORLIST-VERDICT: OK|MISMATCH|FAIL <json path>`.\n22\t\"\"\"\n23\timport argparse, glob, hashlib, json, os, re, shutil, sys, time\n24\t\n25\tHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\n26\tROOT = os.path.dirname(HERE)\n27\tsys.path.insert(0, HERE)\n28\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\"))\n29\t# LAZY LabVIEW IMPORTS (card 81-1, 2026-09-25): the offline re-verdict (`find_reusable` / `reverdict`, used by\n30\t# cycle_runner.errorlist_hook when the bed md5 is unchanged) must import nothing LabVIEW-side, so gscript /\n31\t# lv_errorlist / bench_prep are bound only by `_lv_imports()`, which main() calls first. Same modules, same order.\n32\tg = E = labview_handles = None\n33\tCLAUDEDEV = r\"C:\\Program Files\\National Instruments\\LabVIEW 2026\\user.lib\\claudeDev\"   # == gscript.CLAUDEDEV\n34\t\n35\tEVID = \"user 2026-09-24 error-list check at cycle start\"\n36\t\n37\t\n38\tdef _lv_imports():\n39\t    global g, E, labview_handles\n40\t    if g is None:\n41\t        import gscript as _g\n42\t        import lv_errorlist as _E\n43\t        from bench_prep import labview_handles as _lh\n44\t        g, E, labview_handles = _g, _E, _lh\n45\t        E.EVIDENCE = EVID\n46\t\n47\t\n48\tBENCH = os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\")\n49\t# 2026-09-24 card chat-C2: external search (WebSearch, \"LabVIEW scripting read selected objects block diagram\n50\t# Selection List\") found no route other than a VI Server property node on TopLevelDiagram.Selection List[]; the\n51\t# ActiveX VirtualInstrument interface has no diagram access (toolkit-capabilities.md:666), and building an op VI is\n52\t# outside a labview=read card. So the uid is not read here; the after-capture of the diagram is the record.\n53\tUID_ROUTE = \"none: needs a Selection List[] 6349400 op (unbuilt; card labview=read) - screenshot recorded\"\n54\tCOUNT_RE = re.compile(r\"(\\d+)\\s*errors?\\s*and\\s*warnings?\", re.I)\n55\t\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be8b9dd8-dea4-4521-81a5-108b187601c5","uuid":"1df2a7a0-d44f-4841-a7a3-fd26c93f3bfd","timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:58:36.314Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"G:\\Codes\\LabVIEW_Codes\\MinLab\\zz_LabView VI\\AAA_UNIST\\2. Tracking\\V6_ParallelLoop\\tools\\errorlist_check.py","content":"r\"\"\"errorlist_check - the cycle-start LabVIEW Error List check (user decision 5, 2026-09-24):\n\"사이클 시작하기 전에 LabVIEW 컴파일 에러 창은 반드시 확인해야할듯. GUI로 에러 내용 확인하고 각 에러 더블클릭하면 에러\n위치로 이동해서 보여주거든. (블락 다이어그램 켜진 상태에서)\".\n\nWHAT ALREADY EXISTS (checked first): `tools/lv_errorlist.py` reads every Error List row by capture+OCR, count-checked\nagainst the window's own \"N errors and warnings\" (docs/toolkit-capabilities.md:313; test tools/bench/diag_errorlist_v0.py).\nThis file REUSES it unchanged except for one optional per-item hook (`on_item`), and adds: a byte-identical SCRATCH copy\n(the bed itself is never opened), Ctrl+E so the block diagram is up, a double-click per item with a capture of the\nblock diagram before/after, a zero-item path for a runnable VI, the expected-errors comparison, and the cleanup proofs.\nThe selected object's UID is NOT read: `TopLevelDiagram.Selection List[]` 0x6349400 exists (NI API ref) but the fleet\nhas no op that reads it (`grep \"Selection\" tools/gscript.py` -> 0), and branching `Open VI Reference.vi reference`\ninto a VI-class property node is a MEASURED failure (docs/toolkit-capabilities.md:666). Recorded per item as uid=None.\n\nPREDICTION CONTRACT: Ctrl+E opens '<scratch> Block Diagram'; Ctrl+L opens a new 'Error list' window; items read ==\nthe window's own N (0 for a runnable VI); each double-click fronts the block diagram and changes its capture; the\nError List is closed with Esc; the scratch is closed and deleted; the bed md5 is unchanged; no VI is run or saved.\nEvery GUI act goes through lv_gui.ps1 with -Exception Approved -Evidence EVID (logged to tools/gui_actions.log).\n\n  py tools/errorlist_check.py [--vi <bed.vi>] [--expected <file.json>]      rc 0 OK / 1 MISMATCH / 2 FAIL\n  expected file: {\"expected\": [{\"match\": \"<substring of the row text>\", \"count\": n}, ...]}  (default: none = [])\nLast stdout line: `ERRORLIST-VERDICT: OK|MISMATCH|FAIL <json path>`.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse, glob, hashlib, json, os, re, shutil, sys, time\n\nHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\nROOT = os.path.dirname(HERE)\nsys.path.insert(0, HERE)\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\"))\n# LAZY LabVIEW IMPORTS (card 81-1, 2026-09-25): the offline re-verdict (`find_reusable` / `reverdict`, used by\n# cycle_runner.errorlist_hook when the bed md5 is unchanged) must import nothing LabVIEW-side, so gscript /\n# lv_errorlist / bench_prep are bound only by `_lv_imports()`, which main() calls first. Same modules, same order.\ng = E = labview_handles = None\nCLAUDEDEV = r\"C:\\Program Files\\National Instruments\\LabVIEW 2026\\user.lib\\claudeDev\"   # == gscript.CLAUDEDEV\n\nEVID = \"user 2026-09-24 error-list check at cycle start\"\n\n\ndef _lv_imports():\n    global g, E, labview_handles\n    if g is None:\n        import gscript as _g\n        import lv_errorlist as _E\n        from bench_prep import labview_handles as _lh\n        g, E, labview_handles = _g, _E, _lh\n        E.EVIDENCE = EVID\n\n\nBENCH = os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\")\n# 2026-09-24 card chat-C2: external search (WebSearch, \"LabVIEW scripting read selected objects block diagram\n# Selection List\") found no route other than a VI Server property node on TopLevelDiagram.Selection List[]; the\n# ActiveX VirtualInstrument interface has no diagram access (toolkit-capabilities.md:666), and building an op VI is\n# outside a labview=read card. So the uid is not read here; the after-capture of the diagram is the record.\nUID_ROUTE = \"none: needs a Selection List[] 6349400 op (unbuilt; card labview=read) - screenshot recorded\"\nCOUNT_RE = re.compile(r\"(\\d+)\\s*errors?\\s*and\\s*warnings?\", re.I)\n\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":768}}}
